1jsx|n|A bag or pouch; especially; a small bag inserted in a garment for carrying small articles, particularly money; hence, figuratively, money; wealth. ; One of several bags attached to a billiard table, into which the balls are driven. ; A large bag or sack used in packing various articles, as ginger, hops, cowries, etc. ; A hole or space covered by a movable piece of board, as in a floor, boxing, partitions, or the like. ; A cavity in a rock containing a nugget of gold, or other mineral; a small body of ore contained in such a cavity. ; A hole containing water. ; A strip of canvas, sewn upon a sail so that a batten or a light spar can placed in the interspace. ; Same as Pouch.	a:13r7,77,5;yzh,72,3;22b0,43,5;25l4,22,4;1fju,20,15;ty2,16,2;1vhw,14,10;1tlb,12,4;1obl,11,2;17fg,9,1;16i4,8,7;1hx0,4,2~1fju,20,15;1vhw,14,10;16i4,8,7;22b0,43,5;13r7,77,5;1tlb,12,4;25l4,22,4;yzh,72,3;1hx0,4,2;ty2,16,2;1obl,11,2;17fg,9,1	v:13r7,64,2;yzh,56,1;26mi,47,6;nha,41,2;1m5j,37,4;7qj,19,1;a7s,4,4~26mi,47,6;a7s,4,4;1m5j,37,4;13r7,64,2;nha,41,2;yzh,56,1;7qj,19,1	V:16b9,67,1;jrv,55,1;1v0y,47,5;b1u,43,2;a82,14,1;ay3,13,1;nyv,9,3~1v0y,47,5;nyv,9,3;b1u,43,2;ay3,13,1;16b9,67,1;jrv,55,1;a82,14,1	n:1jo7,96,4;1xe,82,6;13r7,79,6;13jg,75,5;1uay,73,4;92y,73,4;286h,69,4;1o9f,64,3;tco,59,3;1qu6,56,6;23am,44,4;72e,42,3;7qj,42,5;26mi,31,2;22h6,30,1~tgm,26,8;13r7,79,6;1xe,82,6;1qu6,56,6;1td,13,6;1pn4,23,5;7qj,42,5;1t1c,29,5;13jg,75,5;1ukf,7,5;ty2,30,5;17fg,29,4;1t56,11,4;1jo7,96,4;1uay,73,4	N:11j1,107,2;1uwq,96,6;1wpo,93,5;16b9,93,6;16ju,79,3;14le,73,5;1rbi,71,3;285i,62,2;b1u,59,6;k67,59,8;1arn,58,2;a5g,55,5;285e,39,10;jrk,38,1;abs,37,2~285e,39,10;k67,59,8;1ak3,26,7;1uwq,96,6;kl,10,6;16b9,93,6;b1u,59,6;a5g,55,5;167g,20,5;14le,73,5;g0f,25,5;1b4b,12,5;1wpo,93,5;9ud,2,5;16w1,21,4
